Founder Bonus System – Detailed Flow
1. Purpose

The Founder Bonus is a special incentive for creators who perform exceptionally in their first 30 days. Only the first 150 qualifying creators can become Founders. Eligible Founders get a 10% bonus on monthly gifter spend (£500–£10,000) from the platform (not from gifters).

All history, progress, and payouts are tracked in a single table. Frontend shows current month progress, profile badge, and announcement. Admin can reject payout with reason (email sent to creator).

2. Key Configuration

Founder Bonus Thresholds

Minimum first 30-day earnings: £2,500

Monthly spend for bonus: £500–£10,000

Bonus %: 10%

Maximum Founder seats: 150

Job schedule

Qualification check: 6th of each month

Payout processing: 7th of each month

Admin options

Can reject payout with reason

Can reduce first 30-day minimum if needed

Frontend

Profile badge for Founders

Announcement area (Homepage or Profile)

Founder Bonus page (shows current month progress)

3. Tables & Relationships
founder_bonus table

Tracks monthly history and payouts.

Columns (suggested structure):

id (PK)

creator_id (FK → users)

month (YYYY-MM)

first_30d_earnings (decimal)

founder_qualified_at (timestamp)

monthly_earnings (decimal)

bonus_amount (decimal)

payout_status (enum: pending / paid / rejected)

payout_date (timestamp)

payout_rejection_reason (string, nullable)

created_at

updated_at

Users table relation:

users.is_founder → boolean, calculated from founder_bonus table (latest month where creator qualified).

4. Workflow – New & Existing Creators
Step 1: Track First 30 Days Earnings

On creator creation, record created_at.

Nightly job calculates first_30d_earnings = SUM(gifter_spend) for first 30 days.

If first_30d_earnings ≥ £2,500 AND Founder seats available, mark as founder_qualified_at = current_date and create a row in founder_bonus table with month = month of qualification.

Update users.is_founder = true.

Step 2: Monthly Bonus Calculation

Nightly job on 6th of each month:

For all active Founders:

Calculate total gifter spend for previous month.

If spend is between £500–£10,000, calculate bonus = 10% × monthly spend.

Store bonus and monthly spend in founder_bonus table (for that month).

If any refunds occurred after previous bonus payout, subtract from next month’s bonus automatically.

Send congratulations email to qualifying Founders with:

Bonus amount

Link to Founder Bonus page

Badge reminder

Step 3: Payout Processing

Job runs 7th of each month:

For rows with bonus_amount > 0 and payout_status = pending:

Attempt payout via Stripe from platform funds.

Update payout_status = paid and payout_date.

If payout fails or admin rejects, set payout_status = rejected and require reason.

Email reason to creator.

Step 4: Profile & Frontend

Profile Badge

Display Founder badge if users.is_founder = true.

Announcement

Show banner/announcement on Homepage/Profile about Founder program.

Founder Bonus Page

Shows current month progress:

Total gifter spend

Bonus earned (if applicable)

Remaining to qualify (if under threshold)

5. Edge Cases & Rules

Founder Seats

Only first 150 creators qualify.

Seats are filled sequentially based on who meets £2,500 first.

If fewer qualify in a month, remaining seats roll over.

Refund Handling

If bonus paid and refunds occur later, deduct from next month bonus.

Admin Override

Admin can reject payout; reason must be stored and emailed.

Admin can reduce minimum first 30-day threshold if needed.

Historic Data

All monthly calculations stored in founder_bonus table.

Frontend shows only current month progress, not historical payouts.

Notifications

Congratulation email when qualifying.

Email on payout rejection.

UI/UX

Theme matched to vintage look.

Clear messaging for qualifying and bonus progress.

6. AI Implementation Notes

No new migrations besides founder_bonus table.

Jobs: 6th = qualification, 7th = payout.

Stripe metadata: store creator_id, month, bonus_amount, payout_status, payout_date.

All calculations must be idempotent (re-running jobs should not double count).

Deliverables table is checked to confirm gifter spend, no new frontend admin required.



